1
00:00:31,923 --> 00:01:14,449
Full of Surprises

2
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:18,267
Hello. What can I do for you?

3
00:01:18,267 --> 00:01:19,927
Hi. Fill 'er up.

4
00:01:19,927 --> 00:01:21,165
I need a full tank.

5
00:01:21,165 --> 00:01:23,445
Check the hood?

6
00:01:23,445 --> 00:01:33,645
No, thanks.

7
00:01:33,645 --> 00:01:34,733
Whereabouts are you headed?

8
00:01:34,733 --> 00:01:37,295
Pete Waters's farm, near Chesterton.

9
00:01:37,295 --> 00:01:38,947
I know it well.

10
00:01:38,947 --> 00:01:41,551
Pete Waters's lived around here almost as long as I have.

11
00:01:41,551 --> 00:01:45,125
How long is it going to take for me to get there?

12
00:01:45,125 --> 00:01:46,416
About fifteen minutes.

13
00:01:46,416 --> 00:01:48,921
There's a shortcut--if you know it.

14
00:01:48,921 --> 00:01:50,185
No, I don't.

15
00:01:50,185 --> 00:01:53,663
Could you tell me how to use the shortcut?

16
00:01:53,663 --> 00:01:55,996
Sure. You take the next left turn.

17
00:01:55,996 --> 00:01:57,740
You'll see a stop sign.

18
00:01:57,740 --> 00:02:01,358
Make a right at the stop sign.

19
00:02:01,358 --> 00:02:04,361
Stay on that road, and you'll cross a blue bridge.

20
00:02:04,361 --> 00:02:06,778
Then you'll see a big old red barn.

21
00:02:06,778 --> 00:02:12,230
That's the back of Pete Waters's place.

22
00:02:12,230 --> 00:02:16,986
That's quite a difference from the directions that Pete sent me.

23
00:02:16,986 --> 00:02:19,786
Now, if you take that route, it's probably a lot simpler,

24
00:02:19,786 --> 00:02:23,942
but it'll take you ten minutes longer.

25
00:02:23,942 --> 00:02:30,071
OK. Let me repeat it.

26
00:02:30,071 --> 00:02:37,187
I take the next left turn to the stop sign.

27
00:02:37,187 --> 00:02:46,766
Then a right across a blue bridge,

28
00:02:46,766 --> 00:02:50,880
and then a big red barn.

29
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:51,732
Can't miss it.

30
00:02:51,732 --> 00:02:56,700
How much do I owe you?

31
00:02:56,700 --> 00:03:11,056
Well, that'll be eighteen dollars and seventy cents.

32
00:03:11,056 --> 00:03:55,659
No charge for the cleanup.

33
00:03:55,659 --> 00:04:10,149
It's on the house.

34
00:04:10,149 --> 00:04:12,149
Well, here's a twenty.

35
00:04:12,149 --> 00:04:18,891
Ah. OK. That's a dollar and thirty cents change.

36
00:04:18,891 --> 00:04:20,583
There we go ... will make twenty. Thanks.

37
00:04:20,583 --> 00:04:21,083
Thank you.

38
00:04:21,083 --> 00:05:07,730
And thanks for the directions.

39
00:05:07,730 --> 00:05:21,906
This must be Pete's barn.

40
00:05:21,906 --> 00:05:25,782
Turn right to the house.

41
00:05:25,782 --> 00:05:26,078
Hi.

42
00:05:26,078 --> 00:05:28,307
Hi. What can I do for you?

43
00:05:28,307 --> 00:05:33,532
Is this the Pete Waters farm?

44
00:05:33,532 --> 00:05:34,282
It is.

45
00:05:34,282 --> 00:05:40,039
I'm a friend of Pete's.

46
00:05:40,039 --> 00:05:42,865
I'm looking for the house.

47
00:05:42,865 --> 00:05:45,443
It's just over yonder.

48
00:05:45,443 --> 00:06:00,833
Keep along this road

49
00:06:00,833 --> 00:06:05,009
till you get to the end of the fence.

50
00:06:05,009 --> 00:06:06,071
You'll see the chicken house.

51
00:06:06,071 --> 00:06:19,268
His house is on the left.

52
00:06:19,268 --> 00:06:19,694
Well, thanks.

53
00:06:19,694 --> 00:06:30,113
"Have gone to the railroad station.

54
00:06:30,113 --> 00:06:42,025
Back soon with a surprise.

55
00:06:42,025 --> 00:06:43,209
Make yourself at home.

56
00:06:43,209 --> 00:06:50,958
Have a look around. Pete.

57
00:06:50,958 --> 00:06:52,158
Same old Pete Waters.

58
00:06:52,158 --> 00:06:55,158
Always full of surprises.
